2513u.bin 2513 upper case image found on the net
2513l.bin 2513 lower case image found on the net

	each contains 4 duplicate images of ROM
	ROM should only be 512bytes (64*8) but is 2048bytes

	Note 2513l character positions are inverted 
	FF is in location 00
	FE is in location 01
	...
	00 is in location FF
	Rows are OK



upper is proper 2513 upper case image
lower is proper 2513 lower case image

2513_combined = lower + upper concatenated

flip.c used to cleanup 2513l

makerom.c produces left justified (upper 5 bits) ascii character generator rom
first 0x20 location blank etc


2026-10-08 (Claude, for the 6845 Rev B card):
goodfont = makerom.c's output from 2513_combined, byte for byte. It is the 6845 Rev B character EPROM:
128 characters in ASCII order (00-1F blank, 20-3F punctuation and digits, 40-5F @A-Z, 60-7F lower case),
8 rows each, address = character * 8 + row, dots left-justified in bits 7-3 (Rev B's 74166 takes the
2732's O3-O7; O7 is the leftmost dot). Rev B wires character bit 6 to the 2732's A9 and ties A10/A11 low,
so burn goodfont at 000h. makerom2.c's output (96 characters, upper case only, rows moved down one) and
the raw 2513 images do not fit Rev B.
